// dna/tests/graph_model_test.hl — the repository as one hypergraph in the
// record, projected into memory (GH #1085).
//
// The record is written with the graph voice's GRAPH.md lists "as they
// stand" — the nodes and the hyperedges — plus its holes filled (a board,
// a dev and a reviewer under every process, an operator under compose,
// who holds them and what they sign), and three of its practices as
// knowledge ideas, two of them ratified and bound. The tail projects it,
// and memory answers with GRAPH.md's counts and both perspectives: the
// org chart and the process model. A row re-put replaces its edge's
// members, a retired one leaves, and a malformed one stops the projection
// at its row with the reason. The checks on rows run without memory;
// memory is Postgres, and without the owner's DSN in
// HALE_DNA_MEMORY_DSN_OWNER the projection half is not exercised.

import "../core" as dna;
import "../operations" as ops;

// GRAPH.md at hale-lang/voice 98ecf78, "The nodes, as they stand" and
// "The edges, as they stand", one row per line: `N|kind|name|text` or
// `E|kind|role=node|…|via=…|outside=…`. Practices are not here: they are
// knowledge ideas (below).
const VOICE: String = "N|purpose|voice|one inference endpoint over many backends, standalone, with its own admin UI
N|axiom|1|The caller API is an open standard (Open Responses).
N|axiom|2|Voice extends the standard only in the ways it allows.
N|axiom|3|Chat Completions is a compatibility surface.
N|axiom|4|Every request belongs to one project and one key.
N|axiom|5|Responses report what actually served them.
N|axiom|6|Callers never name a node; they may name the account that pays.
N|axiom|7|Nothing is discovered; everything that serves is configured.
N|axiom|8|The node decides what is possible; the coordinator decides what runs.
N|axiom|9|Local controls only restrict.
N|axiom|10|The protocol and the node plane are the seam.
N|axiom|11|One admin UI, served by the api from its own origin; the api is the trust boundary.
N|axiom|12|Only the api is exposed; NATS and the nodes are on the private network.
N|axiom|13|The MVP runs the real process model.
N|axiom|14|State never travels as events; it stays in Postgres.
N|axiom|15|Real development is delivered through a DNA organization.
N|axiom|16|No bypass flags for agent CLIs.
N|process|api|
N|process|brain|
